      "message": "Hi,\n\nPackMidx.getObjectSizeIndexCount() throws UnsupportedOperationException,\nbut its base class Pack returns 0 when there is no object size index.\n\nGC.getStatistics() calls this for every pack without checking\nhasObjectSizeIndex() first, so computing repository statistics on any\nrepo with a multi-pack-index fails with an exception.\n\nI hit this in production: with midx enabled, GC could not complete,\npack files grew from a few to 400+, and 30k+ loose objects accumulated,\neventually causing code fetch failures and missing object errors.\n\nFix: return 0, following the base class contract. A midx never has an\nobject size index.",
